WEBVTT

00:09.460 --> 00:12.290
<b>Greetings, my goddess. 
I am honored to be in your presence.</b>

00:13.980 --> 00:16.220
<b>Pleasure to meet you, Seven Star.</b>

00:16.220 --> 00:20.090
<b>I am Kugasaki Seiran, the first man 
who shall make you kneel down.</b>

00:20.090 --> 00:22.740
<b>Huh. So what do you want?</b>

00:23.160 --> 00:25.130
<b>Your powers defeated my goddess.</b>

00:25.130 --> 00:27.750
<b>If they aren't a sham, 
I'd like to see them one more time!</b>

00:27.970 --> 00:31.330
<b>Hah. So you're here to 
request a game against me?</b>

00:31.330 --> 00:35.510
<b>More specifically, I simply wish 
to prove how far above you I am.</b>

00:36.450 --> 00:39.330
<b>If that's your idea of a joke, 
you need better material.</b>

00:39.820 --> 00:41.890
<b>I'll take you on under one condition.</b>

00:41.890 --> 00:43.150
<b>Shinohara?</b>

00:43.800 --> 00:48.990
<b>Whoever loses the game can never again
challenge the Empress, Saionji Sarasa.</b>

00:49.890 --> 00:54.910
<b>How dare you use my virtuous 
goddess as fodder for your bet!</b>

00:54.910 --> 00:56.870
<b>Don't like it? Challenge someone else.</b>

00:57.300 --> 00:59.660
<b>Nobody would blame you for chickening out.</b>

00:59.660 --> 01:01.200
<b>Chicken out?</b>

01:01.200 --> 01:02.740
<b>I am no mere Five Star.</b>

01:02.740 --> 01:05.660
<b>I am the leader of the Self-Made
Holy Knight Brigade, Kugasaki Seiran!</b>

01:06.880 --> 01:11.370
<b>Shinohara Hiroto! Accept my challenge
for a game in two days' time, on Sunday!</b>

01:11.670 --> 01:17.190
<b>Hah. Fine by me. I'll teach you 
<i>exactly</i> what level you're at, flunky.</b>

02:53.770 --> 02:58.780
<b>A Dead Heat 
and Determination</b>

03:01.000 --> 03:02.230
<b>Oh, good.</b>

03:02.490 --> 03:04.190
<b>It <i>is</i> you, Shinohara.</b>

03:04.550 --> 03:06.960
<b>I was worried you might be someone else.</b>

03:07.270 --> 03:10.940
<b>You say that, but you're the one 
who looks totally different.</b>

03:10.940 --> 03:11.790
<b>Oh? Really?</b>

03:12.430 --> 03:14.050
<b>You look like a suspicious person.</b>

03:17.470 --> 03:21.310
<b>About that thing yesterday...
Did you do that for me?</b>

03:22.130 --> 03:25.940
<b>No, that's not why. 
It was only to protect my lie.</b>

03:25.940 --> 03:29.880
<b>Well, that's a letdown. 
You really are a thoughtless dummy.</b>

03:30.280 --> 03:32.200
<b>But thank you.</b>

03:32.390 --> 03:33.190
<b>Huh?</b>

03:33.390 --> 03:37.690
<b>Anyway, you know the situation. 
Our lies are inextricably linked now.</b>

03:38.060 --> 03:40.950
<b>That's why we're having 
this strategy meeting, right?</b>

03:45.410 --> 03:47.710
<b>Welcome home, Master.</b>

03:47.710 --> 03:49.460
<b>Welcome, Miss.</b>

03:49.770 --> 03:50.590
<b>I'm home.</b>

03:50.590 --> 03:52.270
<b>Wh-Whoa!</b>

03:52.270 --> 03:54.090
<b>Why is that girl here?</b>

03:54.680 --> 03:57.430
<b>Himeji, do you know who this really is?</b>

03:57.430 --> 04:01.560
<b>Yes. I served the Saionji family previously.</b>

04:01.560 --> 04:03.050
<b>Huh? Does that mean...</b>

04:03.050 --> 04:07.050
<b>I am one of the very few people 
who knows Miss Rina's secret.</b>

04:09.010 --> 04:12.410
<b>Uh, well... Good to see you, Yuki.</b>

04:12.790 --> 04:13.560
<b>Indeed.</b>

04:13.940 --> 04:16.140
<b>It has been a year since 
we last met in person.</b>

04:16.140 --> 04:19.310
<b>A year? Guess it has. You been good?</b>

04:19.820 --> 04:24.040
<b>I suppose. Although I did endure 
a period of psychological distress.</b>

04:24.830 --> 04:26.330
<b>Please, come into this room.</b>

04:26.740 --> 04:30.910
<b><i>Oh, that's right. The real Sarasa 
was kidnapped a year ago.</i></b>

04:32.550 --> 04:35.090
<b>This is the game 
Kugasaki-sama has requested.</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>The Self-Made</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>The Self-Made</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>27-Form</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>27-Form</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>Game</b>

04:35.080 --> 04:38.090
<b>Game</b>

04:35.750 --> 04:37.740
<b>"The Self-Made 27-Form Game."</b>

04:38.100 --> 04:41.600
<b>In short, a game where you collect 
cards and compete for numbers.</b>

04:41.600 --> 04:43.060
<b>Compete for numbers?</b>

04:43.060 --> 04:43.590
<b>Yes.</b>

04:43.850 --> 04:47.100
<b>The game is divided into two phases.</b>

04:47.090 --> 04:49.600
<b>Collection Phase</b>

04:47.090 --> 04:49.600
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:47.090 --> 04:49.600
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:47.090 --> 04:49.600
<b>Collection Phase</b>

04:47.100 --> 04:49.330
<b>The first is the collection phase.</b>

04:49.600 --> 04:56.600
<b>Collection</b>

04:49.600 --> 04:56.600
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:49.600 --> 04:56.600
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

04:49.600 --> 04:56.600
<b>Collection</b>

04:50.250 --> 04:54.440
<b>Players must search for cards numbered 
0 to 19 that are scattered around District 4,</b>

04:54.440 --> 04:56.610
<b>then select a hand of
 five cards maximum.</b>

04:56.610 --> 04:59.600
<b>So we basically walk 
around looking for cards?</b>

04:59.600 --> 05:02.850
<b>No, you may also use public transport.</b>

05:02.860 --> 05:16.750
<b>Collection</b>

05:02.860 --> 05:16.750
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:02.860 --> 05:16.750
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:02.860 --> 05:16.750
<b>Collection</b>

05:03.460 --> 05:05.190
<b>Five cards are placed randomly,</b>

05:04.400 --> 05:05.570
<b><b>Start: 5 Cards</b></b>

05:05.190 --> 05:09.180
<b>then every five minutes, 
a new card location is displayed.</b>

05:05.950 --> 05:08.740
<b><b>Mins</b></b>

05:06.700 --> 05:08.740
<b><b>Mins</b></b>

05:07.410 --> 05:08.740
<b><b>Mins</b></b>

05:09.120 --> 05:16.750
<b>The Self-Made 27-Form Game</b>

05:09.590 --> 05:15.180
<b>So if you go to a location with your Device,
you collect the corresponding card, right?</b>

05:15.180 --> 05:16.750
<b>That is correct, Miss Rina.</b>

05:17.140 --> 05:19.240
<b>Okay, so what's the second phase?</b>

05:19.240 --> 05:22.260
<b>The direct confrontation. 
The reveal phase.</b>

05:19.250 --> 05:22.250
<b>Reveal Phase</b>

05:19.250 --> 05:22.250
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:19.250 --> 05:22.250
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:19.250 --> 05:22.250
<b>Reveal Phase</b>

05:22.250 --> 05:30.260
<b>Reveal</b>

05:22.250 --> 05:30.260
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:22.250 --> 05:30.260
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

05:22.250 --> 05:30.260
<b>Reveal</b>

05:23.420 --> 05:28.110
<b>One by one, you choose a card you obtained,
 and the card with the higher number wins.</b>

05:28.110 --> 05:30.250
<b>Though it is limited to a five-card hand.</b>

05:30.790 --> 05:34.010
<b>So to win, you need at least three points.</b>

05:34.010 --> 05:38.030
<b>Yes. And I must explain one other 
thing before we discuss strategy.</b>

05:39.210 --> 05:40.460
<b>In the past,</b>

05:40.460 --> 05:43.880
<b>there have been many games with level gaps,
like your Five Star versus One Star game,</b>

05:43.880 --> 05:46.830
<b>but there is no record of 
a One Star ever winning.</b>

05:47.820 --> 05:49.060
<b>Not even one?</b>

05:49.480 --> 05:52.320
<b>Even though Academy Island's 
been around for 20 years?</b>

05:52.320 --> 05:54.030
<b>It's just like Yuki said.</b>

05:54.300 --> 05:59.410
<b>Shinohara, do you remember the ability I used
in our first game, Numerical Adjustment?</b>

05:59.410 --> 06:02.960
<b>Yeah. The one that reduced my turn
 to 1/10th the normal time.</b>

06:02.960 --> 06:05.820
<b>It allows you to mess with 
numerical values in a game.</b>

06:06.050 --> 06:08.970
<b>So even though the largest value 
you can get here is 19,</b>

06:08.970 --> 06:11.790
<b>at Kugasaki's rank, 
he can increase that to 30.</b>

06:11.790 --> 06:12.980
<b>W-Wait, 30?!</b>

06:12.980 --> 06:17.840
<b>Typically, the lower-ranked student 
is allowed to finalize the game settings.</b>

06:18.280 --> 06:20.870
<b>But I have to forfeit that.</b>

06:20.870 --> 06:24.560
<b>To be blunt, you do not even 
have a 1% chance of winning.</b>

06:24.980 --> 06:26.580
<b>So 100% chance I'll lose?</b>

06:27.290 --> 06:28.940
<b>But that can't be right, is it?</b>

06:28.940 --> 06:32.330
<b>Correct. The trick to winning this game
 is in the collection phase.</b>

06:33.650 --> 06:36.330
<b>You can obstruct Kugasaki-sama's 
movements to buy time</b>

06:36.330 --> 06:39.830
<b>and assemble a hand that will win 
even if Numerical Adjustment is used.</b>

06:40.190 --> 06:43.250
<b>If he comes into the reveal phase 
fully prepared,</b>

06:43.250 --> 06:45.470
<b>it's checkmate for you.</b>

06:46.170 --> 06:50.220
<b>Kugasaki always uses the 
Emergency Mobilization ability.</b>

06:50.220 --> 06:54.290
<b>Of course, it's fundamentally forbidden 
for third parties to get involved in a game,</b>

06:54.290 --> 06:57.320
<b>but those summoned with Emergency 
Mobilization are treated as players</b>

06:57.320 --> 06:59.970
<b>and can even contribute one ability.</b>

07:00.290 --> 07:04.740
<b>And Kugasaki leads the Self-Made Holy
Knight Brigade that has over 300 members.</b>

07:04.740 --> 07:08.290
<b>So basically, he can bring something 
like 300 people into the game?</b>

07:08.850 --> 07:11.490
<b>But this third ability is one
you can ignore.</b>

07:11.490 --> 07:12.730
<b>Oh, really?</b>

07:12.730 --> 07:16.360
<b>You saw Kugasaki use the 
Indigo Star's ability, remember?</b>

07:16.710 --> 07:18.880
<b>Oh. Right.</b>

07:19.540 --> 07:22.300
<b>That one with all the smoke and lightning.</b>

07:23.080 --> 07:25.330
<b>Is that the one called "Black Wings"?</b>

07:25.620 --> 07:30.520
<b>Ever since he got that colored star, 
he's never disabled that ability.</b>

07:30.520 --> 07:34.470
<b>Kugasaki's ability selection will be 
Numerical Adjustment and Black Wings.</b>

07:34.470 --> 07:37.640
<b>Plus, something like 
Emergency Mobilization.</b>

07:38.450 --> 07:40.550
<b>So what would you do, Saionji?</b>

07:41.220 --> 07:45.420
<b>I'd probably use Manipulate Location 
Coordinates to rewrite Device coordinates.</b>

07:45.420 --> 07:46.940
<b>Manipulate Location Coordinates?</b>

07:46.940 --> 07:57.620
<b>Manipulate Location Coordinates</b>

07:46.940 --> 07:57.620
<b>Manipulate Location Coordinates</b>

07:47.480 --> 07:50.190
<b>It makes the Device think
 you're at a card's location,</b>

07:50.190 --> 07:52.490
<b>so you can pick up numbers
 without going to them.</b>

07:52.490 --> 07:54.240
<b>Th-That's an actual ability?</b>

07:54.240 --> 07:57.130
<b>You can only install it 
if you're Five Stars or above.</b>

07:55.030 --> 07:57.620
<b>5 Stars or Above</b>

07:55.030 --> 07:57.620
<b>5 Stars or Above</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:04.460
<b>Explore</b>

07:57.990 --> 08:04.460
<b>Explore</b>

07:58.010 --> 08:04.100
<b>Another idea might be the Explore ability 
to look up all card locations at the start.</b>

08:04.460 --> 08:08.390
<b>But District 4's so big, 
that probably wouldn't be realistic.</b>

08:08.740 --> 08:09.460
<b>Say, Himeji.</b>

08:09.460 --> 08:14.360
<b>Are there any One Star abilities
that may prove handy in this game?</b>

08:14.360 --> 08:17.340
<b>In this case, I wonder if 
Display Bug might be appropriate.</b>

08:18.090 --> 08:21.840
<b>I see. That one makes the 
opponent's Device screen glitch out.</b>

08:22.140 --> 08:25.870
<b>For the second slot, the Luck ability 
might help to even the odds.</b>

08:26.270 --> 08:30.280
<b>It improves the chances of 
higher-numbered cards appearing closer.</b>

08:30.830 --> 08:33.120
<b>And I guess Numerical 
Adjustment in the last slot.</b>

08:33.520 --> 08:37.020
<b>This may be presumptuous, but since 
the true battle is in the collection phase,</b>

08:37.020 --> 08:38.800
<b>I question if it will be effective.</b>

08:39.380 --> 08:42.250
<b>True. But maybe we can 
think of it as insurance.</b>

08:42.610 --> 08:44.150
<b>Very well.</b>

08:45.040 --> 08:47.770
<b>Numerical Adjustment, 
Luck, and Display Bug.</b>

08:47.770 --> 08:50.960
<b>With what I can use now, 
that's probably the best strategy I have.</b>

08:56.990 --> 08:59.400
<b>Why have you been avoiding her?</b>

08:59.750 --> 09:03.360
<b>Actually, Rina is the one 
who has been avoiding me.</b>

09:03.360 --> 09:05.080
<b>"Rina"? Kinda informal.</b>

09:05.980 --> 09:10.880
<b>I used to see her every day. 
She was my closest companion.</b>

09:10.880 --> 09:12.510
<b>Why, then?</b>

09:12.930 --> 09:17.750
<b>I think Rina may be hiding something 
from me and the Saionji family.</b>

09:18.280 --> 09:21.510
<b>I wish for you to protect her, Master.</b>

09:22.120 --> 09:24.500
<b>She is actually quite a fragile girl.</b>

09:27.610 --> 09:33.460
<b>All righty! The collection phase of the 
Self-Made 27-Form Game starts now, meow!</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>The Self-Made</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>The Self-Made</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>27-Form</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>27-Form</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>Game</b>

09:27.620 --> 09:31.210
<b>Game</b>

09:33.460 --> 09:34.170
<b>Yeah!</b>

09:33.460 --> 09:35.590
<b>Kugasaki!</b>

09:34.170 --> 09:36.140
<b>Seven Star!</b>

09:35.580 --> 09:37.590
<b><i>These things always get intense.</i></b>

09:38.440 --> 09:40.220
<b><i>Connection established.</i></b>

09:40.220 --> 09:41.070
<b>Okay.</b>

09:41.640 --> 09:43.300
<b>Display Bug is activated.</b>

09:43.300 --> 09:47.180
<b>And thanks to the Luck ability, 
the higher-numbered cards seem to be nearby.</b>

09:43.310 --> 09:50.190
<b></b>Search Here

09:47.180 --> 09:50.200
<b><i>Yes. First, go to the 14
since it's the closest,</i></b>

09:50.440 --> 09:54.700
<b><i>then compare the 17 to
the next card to plan your route.</i></b>

09:55.410 --> 09:56.690
<b>Roger that.</b>

09:57.050 --> 09:57.920
<b>Go!</b>

09:59.140 --> 10:02.020
<b>But the 17 is kinda far away.</b>

10:02.020 --> 10:05.740
<b><i>That is not a problem. 
I have prepared a fake public bus route.</i></b>

10:05.740 --> 10:07.490
<b>The Company's at it again.</b>

